{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2611 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "3f9318ef2e3828494f5801d66389d41bd672dd41ec3a62029ad4d0b873ae71ca" :edb/db-before-t 2610 :edb/db-after-t 2611 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535923 50 #inst "2026-10-15T08:13:25.731Z" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186124471 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542514 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186124471 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542527 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186124471 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542538 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186124471 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542540 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186124471 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542541 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186124471 1038 #edb/ref 17592186542549 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186124471 1040 #edb/ref 17592186542556 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542514 1068 #edb/ref 17592186542551 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542514 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542514 1071 "Compute the rate of change of the function $f(x,y,z)=3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)=⟨- 3 t,3,\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩$ at the point $t=2.$" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542514 1072 #uuid "034848a3-a1f9-5d8f-b396-bccbb706e96e" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542514 1074 "The rate of change of $f(x,y,z)$ with respect to $t$ along the curve $r(t)$ is given by $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))].$ To calculate this, we can use the chain rule.\n\nThe chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))]=∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3}),\\frac{∂}{∂z}(3 x z^{2} - 3 y^{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 z^{2},- 9 y^{2},6 x z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x=- 3 t$, $y=3$, $z=\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}$ into the above to find $∇f(r(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(r(t)) & =⟨3 \\left(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)^{2},- 9 \\cdot 3^{2},6 \\left(- 3 t\\right) \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $r(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(- 3 t),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(t))] & =∇f(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =⟨3 t^{2} - 9,-81,- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,0,\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\left(3 t^{2} - 9\\right)\\cdot \\left(-3\\right)+\\left(-81\\right)\\cdot \\left(0\\right)+\\left(- 18 t \\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}\\right)\\cdot \\left(\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{t^{2} - 3}}\\right) \\\\  & =- 9 t^{2} + 27+0- 18 t^{2} \\\\  & =- 27 t^{2} + 27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the rate of change of $f$ along the curve $r(t)$ at $t=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(r(2))] & =- 27 (2)^{2} + 27 \\\\  & =-9+0-72 \\\\  & =-81.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542515 1080 "-42" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542515 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542515 1083 #uuid "10a2909f-aed0-5af2-b387-7f8903415e75" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542516 1080 "78" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542516 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542516 1083 #uuid "1553423d-6619-5296-aa27-6dfa538e24eb" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542517 1080 "-24" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542517 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542517 1083 #uuid "1da546db-3c69-539d-8533-ef14ece2b34c" 13194139535923 17592186045443 true] [17592186542518 1080 "-204" 13194139535923 1759218